.TH START-MU2EDAQ-APP 1 "2026" "Mu2e DAQ" "Control Room"
.SH NAME
start\-mu2edaq\-APP \- start a Mu2e DAQ application under the control room
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2edaq\-APP.sh
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR NAME = VALUE ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-foreground ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Standardized start script for a Mu2e DAQ application. It is normally
launched by the control room dispatcher
.BR crs\-app (1)
as
.BR "crs\-app start <app\-id>" ,
which exports
.B CRS_PORT_<NAME>
for each port declared under the app in
.IR apps.yaml .
The script resolves and re\-exports each port, writes a pid file under
.IR $CRS_HOME/run ,
and daemonizes the application, logging to
.IR $CRS_HOME/log/<app\-id>.log .
If the application is already running it exits successfully without
starting a second copy.
.PP
This file is a TEMPLATE: copy it into the application repository, rename
it, and fill in the application identity, its ports, and the launch
command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " NAME=VALUE"
Override a single port. Repeatable. Highest precedence.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Source
.I FILE
(KEY=VALUE shell assignments such as
.BR CRS_PORT_HTTP=5001 )
before resolving ports. Also read from
.BR CRS_APP_CONFIG .
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Run in the foreground (exec the app) instead of daemonizing; useful
under a process supervisor or for debugging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH "PORT PRECEDENCE"
Highest wins:
.BR \-\-port " > " "CRS_PORT_<NAME> environment" " > " "\-\-config file" " > built\-in default."
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_<NAME>
Port assignments injected by
.BR crs\-app (1)
from
.IR apps.yaml .
.TP
.B CRS_HOME
Control room home (default
.IR ~/controlroom ).
Sets the run and log directories unless
.B CRS_RUN_DIR
or
.B CRS_LOG_DIR
override them.
.TP
.B CRS_APP_CONFIG
Default config file when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $CRS_HOME/run/<app\-id>.pid
Pid file, consumed by
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-APP (1).
.TP
.I $CRS_HOME/log/<app\-id>.log
Daemon stdout/stderr.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success or when already running; non\-zero on failure.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-APP (1),
.BR crs\-app (1),
.BR crs\-tunnel (1)
